# armour/shared/pauldron_plate_l: the medium plate pauldron on the left shoulder (plate.3; P2c slice, re-shaded by
# LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.6 / 27.5): the right one's cop and lame, lit from the top-left as it falls on this side.
# Finish regions: R the lame's hem, P the cop's face, N the seam, W a spot on the shadow side. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) a step-4 specular on the lit top of the first scales / lames / plates (top-left light):
# with no step 4 a coloured alloy read as clay; the glint and the dark core make any metal read as metal.
use person
role pauldron plate.3
layer armNear
anchor shoulderL
keys pauld
z 5
side L

